    pr_ref:  # 8e1d
    description: "- **Subject:** The routes command's provenance footer reports a content-hash-cached sibling path rather than the requested input.\n- **Mechanic:** The routes command content-hash-keys its cache. When a byte-identical file is already cached at another path, the provenance footer reports that first-cached path instead of the path actually passed via the input argument. (INVALIDATION-RISK: this depends on a content-identical sibling being cached elsewhere; the route content itself is correct.)\n- **Expectation:** The provenance footer should report the path the user actually requested.\n- **Scope:** The command found the 8 routes correctly (including the WS route) but its footer named a different (byte-identical) sibling file than the one passed as input; stable across re-runs.\n- **Exposure:** A consumer reading the provenance footer to learn which file produced the output, when a content-identical copy is cached at another path.\n- **Consequence:** The consumer is told a path that does not correspond to its own argument, so provenance-tracking or source-trail logic records the wrong source file.\n\n---\n\n(Filed from dogfooding.)"  # 8e1d
    fields: {}  # 8e1d
- op: discuss  # 6214
